{"type":"frame-snapshot","snapshot":{"callId":"kluo@2959","phase":"after","pageId":"page@414c52c88a596e9ac3966c0539c227d6","frameId":"frame@b069dd33a53f2a21471de3c9445cf06d","frameUrl":"http://127.0.0.1:4173/","doctype":"html","html":["HTML",{"__playwright_scroll_top_":"2644","lang":"en"},[[71,10]],[[85,19]],["BODY",{},[[85,20]],["DIV",{"id":"root"},["DIV",{"class":"app-shell","data-reduced-motion":"true"},[[85,22]],[[77,5]],["MAIN",{"id":"main","class":"main-content "},["SECTION",{"class":"interior-screen"},[[71,12]],[[82,10]],[[74,10]],["DIV",{"class":"inspection","data-mission":"ingenuity"},[[69,1]],["SECTION",{"class":"quest-header","aria-label":"Ingenuity investigation"},["DIV",{"class":"quest-heading-row"},["DIV",{},["P",{"class":"eyebrow"},[[60,0]],[[60,1]],"2",[[60,3]],[[60,4]]],["H2",{"tabindex":"-1"},"Flight in Thin Air"]],[[60,10]]],["OL",{"class":"quest-progress","aria-label":"Mission progress","style":"--quest-count: 6;"},[[3,3]],["LI",{"data-state":"active","aria-current":"step"},[[60,20]],["SPAN",{},[[60,21]],["SMALL",{},"active"]]],[[60,32]],[[60,39]],[[60,46]],[[60,53]]],["P",{"class":"quest-opening"},"The blades look large beside the body. On Mars, that relationship was a practical answer to a difficult atmosphere."],["DETAILS",{"class":"listen-mode"},[[60,60]],["P",{},[[60,61]],"Flight in Thin Air",[[60,63]]],[[60,68]],[[60,75]],[[60,77]],[[60,90]],[[60,93]],[[60,95]]],["OL",{"class":"objective-tracker","aria-label":"Current objectives"},["LI",{"data-done":"false"},["SPAN",{"aria-hidden":"true"},"○"],"Inspect Counter-rotating rotors",["SPAN",{"class":"sr-only"}," required"]],["LI",{"data-done":"false"},["SPAN",{"aria-hidden":"true"},"○"],"Collect Less air, less lift",["SPAN",{"class":"sr-only"}," required"]],["LI",{"data-done":"false"},["SPAN",{"aria-hidden":"true"},"○"],"Collect Two rotors, opposite directions",["SPAN",{"class":"sr-only"}," required"]],["LI",{"data-done":"false"},["SPAN",{"aria-hidden":"true"},"○"],[[60,117]]]],[[60,121]],[[18,1]]],[[69,20]],[[51,4]],["SECTION",{"id":"quest-workbench","class":"quest-workbench","aria-label":"Evidence and reconstruction"},[[34,9]],["DIV",{"class":"evidence-grid"},["DETAILS",{"class":"evidence-card","data-collected":"false"},["SUMMARY",{},"Less air, less lift",["SMALL",{},"Open record"]],["DIV",{"class":"evidence-body"},["P",{"class":"record-context"},"Flight environment · qualitative engineering explanation"],["P",{},"Mars has roughly one percent of Earth’s atmospheric density near the surface. Rotors have much less air to push against. Lower gravity reduces the aircraft’s weight, but does not remove the need to generate lift."],["FIGURE",{"class":"science-diagram"},["svg",{"viewBox":"0 0 360 145","role":"img","aria-label":"Illustrative lift diagram: two stacked rotors turn in opposite directions; lift acts upward and weight downward."},["path",{"d":"M180 40v65M60 60h240M85 82h190","stroke":"#bfced0","stroke-width":"4"}],["path",{"d":"M180 32V8l-6 8m6-8 6 8M180 111v25l-6-8m6 8 6-8M70 43q100-35 220 0l-8-13m8 13-16 2M85 98q95 28 190 0l-7 13m7-13-16-2","stroke":"#eccca0","fill":"none","stroke-width":"2"}],["text",{"x":"196","y":"19"},"Lift"],["text",{"x":"196","y":"135"},"Weight"],["text",{"x":"8","y":"128"},"Opposite rotation"]],["FIGCAPTION",{},"Illustrative engineering diagram. Not to scale; no flight telemetry or numerical simulation."]],["SECTION",{},["H4",{},"A linked design problem"],["P",{},"Large, rapidly turning blades and a lightweight vehicle help address the thin atmosphere. These choices work together. Lower gravity helps; it does not make a heavy vehicle with small, slow blades a safe substitute."]],["P",{"class":"record-relevance"},["STRONG",{},"Why it matters:"]," ","The diagram shows relationships, not a calculator for real flight performance. No numerical flight physics is simulated."],["UL",{"class":"evidence-sources"},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.jpl.nasa.gov/news/press_kits/ingenuity/landing/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL · Original demonstration objectives"," ",["SPAN",{"class":"sr-only"},"(opens in a new tab)"]]]],["BUTTON",{"class":"text-button"},"Collect evidence: Less air, less lift"]]],["DETAILS",{"class":"evidence-card","data-collected":"false"},["SUMMARY",{},"Two rotors, opposite directions",["SMALL",{},"Open record"]],["DIV",{"class":"evidence-body"},["P",{"class":"record-context"},"Rotor system · lift and control"],["P",{},"Two stacked rotors turn in opposite directions. Their opposing torques help prevent the body from simply spinning the other way. The blades are carbon-fibre structures, not solid heavy metal paddles."],["SECTION",{},["H4",{},"Control is more than speed"],["P",{},"Ingenuity controls flight by adjusting blade pitch: the angle at which blades meet the air. That changes lift and allows control of the aircraft. It is misleading to treat it as a consumer drone controlled only by changing motor speeds."]],["P",{"class":"record-relevance"},["STRONG",{},"Why it matters:"]," ","Lift, torque and control solve different parts of the flight problem. The static model shows the engineering arrangement, not a running rotor simulation."],["UL",{"class":"evidence-sources"},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.jpl.nasa.gov/news/press_kits/mars_2020/ingenuity/landing/mission/spacecraft/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL · Spacecraft engineering"," ",["SPAN",{"class":"sr-only"},"(opens in a new tab)"]]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/blog/what-were-learning-about-ingenuitys-flight-control-and-aerodynamic-performance/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Flight control and aerodynamic performance"," ",["SPAN",{"class":"sr-only"},"(opens in a new tab)"]]]],["P",{"class":"record-requirement"},"First inspect ","Counter-rotating rotors"," using its existing hotspot or component list above."],["BUTTON",{"class":"text-button","disabled":""},"Collect evidence: Two rotors, opposite directions"]]]],["DIV",{"clas